  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[4(299) + 3(299) + 2(299) + 298?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2889\\)",
    "B": "\\(2989\\)",
    "C": "\\(2991\\)",
    "D": "\\(2999\\)",
    "E": "\\(3009\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The first three terms give \\(4+3+2=9\\) copies of \\(299\\). Also, \\(298=299-1\\), so adding the last term gives ten copies of \\(299\\), then subtracts \\(1\\). Therefore the value is\n\\[10\\cdot299-1=2990-1=2989.\\]\nThe answer is \\(2989\\), choice B.",
